Package: calypso
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-cairo,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.14), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-poppler-0.18, gir1.2-pango-1.0, qpdf
Recommends: ghostscript, python3-pypdf, libnss3-tools
Description: PDF document viewer for GNOME, with the tools to change them
 Calypso reads PDF documents like GNOME Papers (same engine, Poppler):
 continuous or page-by-page scrolling, two pages side by side, zoom, rotation,
 night mode, presentation mode, thumbnails, outline, search, text selection,
 links with preview, printing, password-protected documents.
 .
 It also annotates (notes, highlight, underline, strike out, shapes), fills in
 forms, verifies and adds digital signatures, and brings the PDF tools of the
 Odysseus file manager: organize pages by dragging thumbnails, merge,
 compress, watermark, redact, protect with a password.
 It follows the desktop theme (Adwaita, light/dark, accent colour).
